      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-182629",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\mid (2, 5)|= c$, complete the following reasoning regarding the cardinality of the set $[2, 5)$:\n\nSince the function $f: x \u2192 x$ (that maps any number to itself) is an injection from $(2, 5)$ into $[2, 5)$, and\n$3$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nis an injection from $[2, 5)$ onto $[2.5, 4)\u2286(2, 5)$, according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schr\u00f6der theorem, we have that\n$\\mid [2, 5)|=$ {{field-3}}."
